No.
I think you are confusing skill (i.e. unskilled, basic, etc) with 
modifiers (i.e. +/- something). The skills are compared, then the 
modifiers are calculated based on the lower skill. AFAIK. Actually, just 
as it says in the paragraphs you quote. 

> And is this why #twoweapon combat only exercises the #twoweapon skill,
> and never the individual weapon skills? After all, given the above,
> the exercise of such skills wouldn't matter.

I think it's a good and common-sense system. What would you otherwsie 
propose? There are many alternate possible systems - excercising both 
skills simultanously (really unbalanced IMHO), excercising both skills 
at 'half speed' (unnecessarily complex IMHO), automatically excercising 
one of the skills (several order variations possible here) until it is 
'maxed' and then swtiching to another (even more complex, and not in 
line with the general skill system IMHO), etc. The way the game 
currently implements it rhymes with my logic, but NHINRL of course so 
everything is possible.

